  "behaviors": [
    {"id":"BEH-001","area":"headers and authentication","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/quickstart#prerequisites","status":"partial","current":"Official-style routes require a bearer token and accept the beta header.","remaining":"Match header requirements, project permission failures, and documented error bodies across every operation."},
    {"id":"BEH-002","area":"agent omitted/null/update semantics","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/configuration#update-a-saved-agent","status":"partial","current":"Saved and inline fields preserve omitted values, replace supplied objects, and reset nulls. Provider requests verify effort, summary, text, and auto/default/flex/priority tiers across cold resume.","remaining":"Session updates change only model, effort, and tier for later turns; prototype limits and provider-specific model compatibility remain."},
    {"id":"BEH-003","area":"metadata constraints","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/configuration","status":"partial","current":"Agent metadata enforces 16 string pairs, 64-character keys, 512-character values; omitted preserves, null/empty clears, supplied objects replace. SDK covers unicode limits and invalid updates.","remaining":"Agents and sessions share one validator; extend it to remaining metadata-bearing resources and project scope."},
    {"id":"BEH-004","area":"cursor pagination","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/sessions/events#fetch-items-and-turns","status":"partial","current":"Agents, sessions, items, and turns support after/order/limit with exclusive cursors that reject unknown or deleted IDs; sessions filter by agent_id.","remaining":"Apply stable created_at plus ID ordering, exclusive cursors, ownership validation, defaults, filters, and 1..100 limits to every list operation; environment files use opaque page tokens."},
    {"id":"BEH-005","area":"session input and idempotency","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/sessions#continue-or-steer-the-work","status":"partial","current":"Batches of 1-32 events are validated whole, then run in order: tool results plus at most one message or cancel. Messages carry text and data-URL images. Idempotency-Key is scoped to the session, retained 24 hours, replays stored outcomes, rejects different reuse (400) and concurrent use (409), and reports interrupted dispatch as unknown (409) without re-running.","remaining":"The public docs define neither batch nor idempotency semantics; these are local decisions pending an upstream contract. Initial input for non-none environments waits for G09."},
    {"id":"BEH-006","area":"stream ordering and recovery","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/sessions/events#how-to-recover-a-disconnected-stream","status":"partial","current":"Streams are live-only and close on lag (1,024-event buffer), backend loss, or session deletion. Items follow the SDK added/part/delta/done order; terminal turns close unfinished items as incomplete; a documented subscribe/read/merge recovery reproduces saved items.","remaining":"Environment/subagent event families and real-provider ordering evidence; never promise replay."},
    {"id":"BEH-007","area":"function required actions and results","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/tools/functions","status":"partial","current":"Pending calls; string or input_text/input_image content-part results; failures as error; 10,000-byte result text (below Codex's truncation); identical-retry receipts; racing results resolve once (409 for the loser); late results after cancellation conflict; batched results; the SDK-recognized pending-call race error; loss-to-unresolved behavior.","remaining":"Deferred functions with tool search, which needs worker-reported model support; the public docs publish no result size limit, so 10,000 bytes is a local decision."},
    {"id":"BEH-008","area":"tool and capability configuration","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/overview#what-the-managed-harness-provides","status":"partial","current":"All pinned SDK tool configuration variants persist and round trip; unsupported execution is rejected explicitly.","remaining":"Execute deferred functions/tool search (G06), public MCP/web (G07), and programmatic calling (G08); retain prototype limits until verified."},
    {"id":"BEH-009","area":"multi-agent orchestration","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/multi-agent","status":"partial","current":"enabled/max_concurrent_subagents persist; enabled defaults concurrency to 6, disabled returns null. Enabled execution is rejected.","remaining":"Implement parent/child execution, ownership, cancellation, persistence, items/turns, events, and usage (G08)."},
    {"id":"BEH-010","area":"environment lifecycle","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/environments/lifecycle","status":"missing","current":"Official-style sessions accept environment none; the prototype has a non-contract read-only local mode.","remaining":"Implement self-hosted attachment first, then managed provisioning; five-minute input-time connection wait, no blind command/input replay, and separate session/compute ownership."},
    {"id":"BEH-011","area":"hosted environment configuration","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/environments/openai-hosted#configure-the-sandbox","status":"missing","current":"No public implementation.","remaining":"Implement packages, setup commands, files, env restrictions, skills/plugins, templates, capability directories, and network enabled/disabled/restricted with 1..100 exact hosts."},
    {"id":"BEH-012","area":"files and artifacts limits","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/environments/files#file-limits","status":"missing","current":"No public implementation.","remaining":"Enforce 50 creation files, 5 MiB inline each, 10 MiB inline total, 50 MiB Files API source, 200 MiB artifact, and 500 MiB published-output total; stream transfers and preserve artifact/session lifetime rules."},
    {"id":"BEH-013","area":"vaults and credentials","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/tools/vaults","status":"missing","current":"Session creation rejects vault_ids.","remaining":"Implement encrypted secret storage, metadata separation, MCP and environment-variable auth variants, OAuth rotation, networking restrictions, attachment, revocation, and redaction."},
    {"id":"BEH-014","area":"webhooks","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/sessions/webhooks","status":"missing","current":"No delivery implementation.","remaining":"Deliver the five inventoried event types with signed payloads, transactional outbox state, documented retry/deduplication behavior, and environment connection data."},
    {"id":"BEH-015","area":"usage accounting","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/observability#understand-token-usage","status":"partial","current":"Turn and session usage are summed from increases in Codex's cumulative token totals, so replays and repeated updates are not double-counted; null until reported; cached and reasoning tokens are included in input and output.","remaining":"Subagent usage (G08) and real-provider verification (G12)."},
    {"id":"BEH-016","area":"trace export","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/tracing#export-session-traces","status":"missing","current":"No public implementation and no Python SDK 3.17.0 resource method.","remaining":"Implement paginated OTLP JSON via raw HTTP and retain a fixture until SDK support exists."},
    {"id":"BEH-017","area":"worker and process recovery","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/overview","status":"partial","current":"Managed startup/shutdown and completed-session resume work. A crashed managed worker restarts with bounded backoff while durable reads keep serving; backend generations are fenced; turns and function results lost to a disconnect are reconciled from rollout history; a worker orphaned by an API crash is reclaimed on Unix.","remaining":"Cover Windows orphan containment, the spawn-to-record window, and environment failure (G09). Lost function waiters become unresolved rather than re-driven."},
    {"id":"BEH-018","area":"provider interoperability","source_url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents-api/environments/self-hosted#sandbox-providers","status":"missing","current":"Provider examples were inventoried as consumers of the common self-hosted contract, not extra public endpoints.","remaining":"Validate the common executor attachment and lifecycle against at least one actual provider; provider selection and billing remain separate decisions."}
  ],
